1. Includes the necessary headers (`<array>` for `std::array` and `<iostream>` for input/output operations).
2. Initializes a `std::array` named `myArray` with 176 elements, all set to zero.
3. Prints the first 10 elements of the array.
4. Prints the last 10 elements of the array.

You can compile and run this code using a C++ compiler to see the output.
